          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.11,
            0.882,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Rehmat’s marks in Maths are as follows: 60% in internal tests, 64% in the project, 73% in the final exam. The annual percentage score is calculated by combining the internals, project, and final exam in the ratio 3 : 2 : 5. What is Rehmat’s annual score in Maths?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.187,
            0.883,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose all modes of assessment had an equal weightage. Then the annual score can be obtained by calculating the arithmetic mean of 60%, 64%, and 73%, which is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{60 + 64 + 73}{3} = 65.6\\%"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.265,
            0.882,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The given ratio 3 : 2 : 5 indicates the relative weightage and importance that each form of evaluation gets. The data with these relative weights is equivalent to 60, 60, 60, 64, 64, 73, 73, 73, 73, 73. The arithmetic mean is given by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{60 \\times 3 + 64 \\times 2 + 73 \\times 5}{10} = 67.3\\%"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.359,
            0.881,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This can also be expressed as a weighted mean of 60%, 64%, 73% with weights 3, 2, 5 respectively:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.405,
            0.779,
            0.476
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{\\left(\\frac{60}{100}\\right) \\times 3+\\left(\\frac{64}{100}\\right) \\times 2+\\left(\\frac{73}{100}\\right) \\times 5}{3+2+5}=\\frac{\\left(\\frac{673}{100}\\right)}{10}=67.3 \\%"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.49,
            0.851,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The weights assigned to the values in any data indicate the relative importance/emphasis that each value gets with respect to the others."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.365,
            0.564,
            0.631,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 10.2"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.612,
            0.883,
            0.727
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Savitri’s marks in Kashmiri are as follows: 35 out of 50 in internal tests, 44 out of 60 in the project, and 80 out of 100 in the final exam. The annual percentage score is calculated by combining the internals, project, and final exam in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. Which of the following expression(s) gives her annual score (as a percentage) in Kashmiri?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.736,
            0.647,
            0.923
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}& (i)  \\quad \\frac{35 \\times 3 + 44 \\times 4 + 80 \\times 5}{3 + 4 + 5} \\\\& (ii)  \\quad \\frac{\\left( \\begin{matrix} \\dfrac{35}{100} \\end{matrix} \\right) \\times 3 + \\left( \\begin{matrix} \\dfrac{44}{100} \\end{matrix} \\right) \\times 4 + \\left( \\begin{matrix} \\dfrac{80}{100} \\end{matrix} \\right) \\times 5}{3 + 4 + 5} \\\\& (iii)  \\quad \\frac{\\left( \\begin{matrix} \\dfrac{35}{50} \\end{matrix} \\right) \\times 3 + \\left( \\begin{matrix} \\dfrac{44}{60} \\end{matrix} \\right) \\times 4 + \\left( \\begin{matrix} \\dfrac{80}{100} \\end{matrix} \\right) \\times 5}{3 + 4 + 5} \\times 100\\end{aligned}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
